course: dictionary
lesson: 10398
title: Rivers and their tributaries
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tributary is a smaller river or stream that flows into a bigger river or a lake. You can work out the meaning from the clues in the sentence: «A tributary is a smaller river or stream that flows into a bigger river.» Smaller, flows into and bigger tell you where a tributary sits.
explain: Geographers describe a river's journey in order. «A river starts at its source, is joined by smaller streams called tributaries, and ends at its mouth.» The tributaries join along the way, so they sit in the middle of the river's journey, between the source and the mouth.
explain: Look for phrases that tell you what a word usually goes with. «Tributary of» means it belongs to a bigger river, as in «a tributary of the Mississippi». «Main river and its tributaries» shows that the main river is the big one and the tributaries are the smaller ones that feed it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The Missouri is a stream that flows into a bigger river» instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A tributary is a river or stream that flows into a bigger river or a lake.
fact: «The Missouri» is a tributary of the Mississippi, and the Ohio is another.
fact: A river's drainage basin is all the land that slopes towards it, so its tributaries carry water from a huge area.
fact: Where two rivers meet is called a confluence.
fact: «Tributaries» is the plural: one tributary, many tributaries.
exercise: «The Missouri is a tributary of the Mississippi.» What is a tributary? | *A river or stream that flows into a bigger river or a lake | A rock that is worn smooth by waves | A mountain that rises above the clouds | A town built beside the sea
exercise: What is the plural of tributary? | tributaryes | *tributaries | tributarys | tributary's
exercise: «A river starts at its source, is joined by smaller streams called tributaries, and ends at its mouth.» Where does a river end? | *At its mouth | At its basin | At its source | At its tributaries
test: Which river is a tributary of the Mississippi? | *Missouri | Nile | Amazon | Thames
test: A place where two rivers meet is called a what? | estuary | *confluence | source | basin
exam: Mina says a tributary flows out to the sea by itself. Is she right? | *No, it flows into a bigger river or a lake | Yes, but only in winter | Yes, it always reaches the sea directly | No, because it has no water
